---
// Review — the workspace's sweep: every project's public page, whether it is
// up to date, and each organization's backlog.
//
// The brief's five (docs/product-brief.md §5):
//
// 1. ONE QUESTION: "Which public pages are behind, and whose sweep has slipped?"
// 2. READERS: an administrator, who answers for every organization's schedule.
//    Hardest: the administrator deciding where to spend an afternoon — the
//    oldest wait first, and the organizations whose schedules are overdue.
//    WHO IS NOT HERE: the editor who made the change; the project page is
//    theirs.
// 3. SERIES/SCALAR: no scalars (user, 2026-11-18: the three figures are
//    gone — the toggle counts, the list sorts oldest first and marks Overdue);
//    the inbox — Proposals / Waiting / Held — with the selected project's Key
//    facts in the rail (user, 2026-11-18). Proposals moved into the inbox from
//    a block above it. No Up to date list and no By organization table (user,
//    2026-11-18): the first figure says how many are done, and each
//    organization's backlog lives on its own Review page.
// 4. IRREVERSIBLE: Publish, one project at a time, with its changes in front
//    of the reader. THE SWEEP HAPPENS HERE (user, 2026-11-17: "admins very
//    rarely will go to an individual project and do that review there"): the
//    waiting list is an inbox, the selected project's review beside it
//    (firma2-review-inbox), Publish and next moving down the list in place.
//    Each project's own review page stays, for links from the project.
// 5. CUT: bulk publish (a publish nobody looked at is the failure this
//    workflow exists to prevent), per-editor scorecards, and a schedule
//    setting — each organization sets its own in Organization settings.
//
// The h1 is not drawn (user, 2026-11-18: "why do we need that big title?"):
// the top bar already names the page, and the figures are the page's top.
//
// Zero page CSS.
import AppLayout from '../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Firma2PageHeader from '../../components/shared/firma2-page-header.astro';
import Firma2ReviewQueue from '../../components/review/firma2-review-queue.astro';
import Firma2ReviewInbox from '../../components/review/firma2-review-inbox.astro';
import Firma2SidePanel from '../../components/shared/firma2-side-panel.astro';
import Firma2ReviewProjectRail from '../../components/review/firma2-review-project-rail.astro';
import { organizationsByProject, workspaceQueue } from '../../data/firma2-publishing';

const queue = workspaceQueue();
---
<!-- manifest:
  layout: stack(xl)
  sections:
    - page header -> firma2-page-header
    - project rail -> firma2-side-panel (firma2-rail) holding firma2-review-project-rail: the selected project's Key facts
    - queue       -> firma2-review-queue (workspace scope: summary, waiting)
      - waiting   -> firma2-review-inbox (slot "waiting": Proposals / Waiting / Held beside the selected item)
-->
<AppLayout title="Review — ProjectFirma 2.0" active="review" width="full">
  <Firma2SidePanel id="review-project" title="Key facts" panelWidth="22rem">
  <Firma2ReviewProjectRail slot="panel" items={queue.pending} />
  <div class="stack" data-gap="lg">
    <Firma2PageHeader title="Review" hideTitle />
    <Firma2ReviewQueue queue={queue} overdueFor={queue.overdueFor} upToDate={false} summary={false} organizationsOf={organizationsByProject()}>
      <Firma2ReviewInbox slot="waiting" items={queue.pending} overdue={new Set(queue.overdueFor.keys())} />
    </Firma2ReviewQueue>
  </div>
  </Firma2SidePanel>
</AppLayout>
